BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-09-30_1758_facebook_where-to-start.md@social-squad-schedule
DTSTAMP:20260930T095800Z
DTSTART:20260930T095800Z
DTEND:20260930T102800Z
SUMMARY:Facebook: Where to start?
DESCRIPTION:approved - Remember the first time you rode a bicycle? Or the f
 irst time you spoke a language that wasn't your mother tongue? Or your fir
 st hour on a computer at school?\n\nNew feels exciting and scary at once. 
 Exciting because it's new. Scary because of everything we don't know yet. 
 But not knowing something doesn't mean we can't learn it\, and the scary p
 art usually shrinks once we look at the details. So let's look.\n\nTake AI
 . The news is loud: it's amazing\, it's exciting\, it's frightening\, some
 times in the same headline.\n\nI'm learning AI in public\, so I started th
 is blog. It's called AI Business Lab.\n\nI work in finance and strategy\, 
 so that's where I start\, not where I stop. I'll test AI on business probl
 ems wherever they show up\, from a budget table to building my own team of
  agents.\n\nI like things structured and easy to follow\, and I'll break d
 own the complex terms and ideas the way I wish someone had done for me.\n\
 nRegularly\, I'll run one real task through AI and show you what happened\
 , mistakes included.\n\nIf you're starting too\, come along. Let's share\,
  help each other and learn together.\n\nCheers!\n\nP.S. This post was co-c
 reated by me and my Social Squad Agent team. I'll introduce them here\, sl
 owly.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
